-- title:
--   Upper bound for the Eisenstein ideal index at level p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and write $\mathbb{T}(p) =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$ generated by the linear operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid p$ together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid p$. Assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralBasis p`](def/CuspForm_IntegralLattice.html#L17): the $\mathbb{C}$-span of those $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients $a_n(f)$ lie in the bottom subring of $\mathbb{C}$ (the image of $\mathbb{Z}$) is all of $S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$. Let `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ be the polynomial ring on the primes, let `heckeProj p` be the ring homomorphism sending $X_\ell \mapsto U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid p$ and $X_\ell \mapsto T_\ell$ otherwise, and let $\mathfrak{I} =$ `eisensteinIdeal p` be the kernel of the evaluation $X_\ell \mapsto 1$ for $\ell \mid p$, $X_\ell \mapsto 1 + \ell$ otherwise. The assertion is that some $i \in \mathfrak{I}$ satisfies $\mathrm{heckeProj}\,p\,(i) = n(p) \cdot 1$ in $\mathbb{T}(p)$, where $n(p) = (p-1)/\gcd(p-1,12)$ is viewed as an integer and mapped in by the structure map $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{T}(p)$.
--
--   This is the upper-bound half of Mazur's computation of the Eisenstein ideal at prime level, namely that the index of the image of the Eisenstein ideal in the weight-two Hecke algebra of $\Gamma_0(p)$ divides the numerator $n(p)$ of $(p-1)/12$. It feeds the statements that $n(p)$ annihilates the quotient up to the relevant scalar action and that the quotient $\mathbb{T}(p)/\mathfrak{I}\mathbb{T}(p)$ has cardinality exactly $n(p)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_mem_eisensteinIdeal_heckeProj_eq_eisensteinNumerator.lean

